msgid "Close a session {#close-a-session}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is good practice to close a `Session` when all jobs are done. This will "
"reduce wait time for subsequent users.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Batch mode with REST API {#batch-mode-with-rest-api}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can submit a batch job by specifying the `mode` in the "
"request payload. Batch mode can help shorten processing time if all jobs can"
" be provided at the outset. Learn about batch mode in the [introduction to "
"execution modes](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode) guide.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Examples of jobs submitted in a session {#examples-of-jobs-submitted-in-a-"
"session}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once a session is set up, one or more Sampler or Estimator jobs can be "
"submitted to the same session by specifying the session ID.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The `<parameter values>` in a `PUB` can either be a single parameter or a list of parameters. It also supports `numpy` broadcasting.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

